later becoming chief research officer at Chicago Options Associates. In 1996, Wales co-founded Bomis, which funded the free peer-reviewed encyclopedia Nupedia (2000–2003). On January 15, 2001, with Larry Sanger and others, he launched Wikipedia, which grew rapidly."},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q181"},{"d":"American author, computer scientist, and homeopath","dl":null,"id":"Q11770","l":"Amy L. Lansky","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1955-01-01T00:00:00Z","occupation":"homeopath"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q11770"},{"d":"American hacker (1963–2023)","dl":null,"id":"Q7449","l":"Kevin Mitnick","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1963-08-06T00:00:00Z","death_date":"2023-07-16T00:00:00Z","occupation":"computer security consultant"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7449"},{"d":"American comedy musician (born 1959)","dl":null,"id":"Q8349","l":"\"Weird Al\" Yankovic","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1959-10-23T00:00:00Z","occupation":"actor"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q8349"},{"d":"American actress, humanitarian and filmmaker (born 1975)","dl":null,"id":"Q13909","l":"Angelina Jolie","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1975-06-04T00:00:00Z","occupation":"actor"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13909"},{"d":"American football player","dl":null,"id":"Q14027","l":"Tony Romo","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1980-04-21T00:00:00Z","occupation":"sports commentator"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q14027"},{"d":"American television director, producer and writer","dl":null,"id":"Q8570","l":"Jonathan Glassner","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"2000-01-01T00:00:00Z","occupation":"screenwriter"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q8570"},{"d":"American actress","dl":null,"id":"Q4518","l":"Alison Lohman","ll":null,"m":{"birth_date":"1979-09-18T00:00:00Z","occupation":"voice actor"},"t":"person","u":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4518"},{"d":"American actress","dl":null,"id":"Q4350","l":"Mel